208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 127 0 R
/E (Panem was founded after a global conflict and resulting series of environmental disasters that largely destroyed the modern world. As rising sea levels caused by extreme global warming flooded coastal cities, the agricultural system that once sustained the United States collapsed, causing the failure of international supply chains and suspending almost all forms of trade. In what was once known as North America, those who survived gradually organized themselves around the arable land, and began building a capital in the Rocky Mountains. Surrounding it were thirteen districts, each responsible for producing resources and technologies required to sustain the nation, which included present-day Mexico, Canada, and the United States.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
