/P 130 0 R
/E (Along with this, security remains one of the most pressing concerns facing the new government. The Peacekeepers, once the primary military and law enforcement force, have been partially disbanded, and their loyalty to the new government remains uncertain. District 2, once serving as the primary military base for Peacekeepers, finds itself in a major predicament; with no need for Peacekeeper training or large-scale weapon manufacturing, many are losing their jobs, and the economy is on the brink of collapse. Additionally, in fear of conflict, several districts have begun establishing their own local defense forces, whereas others are advocating for the reconstruction of a unified national military to ensure stability and prevent secession.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
